  "details": "The android beta has been the only way i can play for months and it has been problematic and stressful\n\nI am using a moto g 84 5G, and the first huge issue is many times when i fully have my earplug headphones in, the game echoes the game audio to the players, no matter if i make it very low sensibility \n\nAnd I played like that for so long, until i figured out it stopped if i only plugged it in halfway, meaning it only works if i plug in improperly, meaning this is the only app i ever had where i had to not use my headphones in a normal way\n\nThen there's the problem with the avatars, for months i had no access to full avatars and non very poor avatars, and i was happy when it finally let me use them, then it suddenly stopped, and all the fun i was having with the avatars other people had was gone\n\nI feel like I'm playing a very broken version and I don't know if anything that i have said has ever reached the developers working on it, i just wanna play the game normally without having to buy a gaming pc just for it, I don't think its fair\n\nI don't understand why turn the ability to fully render avies off? Why would the developers force me to not use the one thing in the game that is truly interesting, which is the fact i can be any character, i know that there is lag and processing issues with many avies, but can't i have the capability of choosing which ones to turn on and which ones to keep low res? I don't see a point in just being forced to not see, even in a beta, i was doing fine choosing which avies to turn on and off, now i can't see most avies\n\nMy phone is the 8gb ram version of fhe motorola g84 5g\n\nThe version that shows in the playstore is 2024.4.2p2-1554-cc1064baea-Release\n\nIt updated recently as of January 12 2025",
